sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-25> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Developmental bioelectrics is an ancient precursor of nervous systems: evolution first used analog bioelectric dynamics to position body configuration in developmental morphospace, long before some cells specialized in fast digital spiking to control behaviour in 3D space.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Developmental bioelectricity preceded and gave rise to nervous systems";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Evolutionary Aspects › Somatic Bioelectrics Reveals the Origin of Complex Cognitive Systems”. Scope: Evolution of bioelectric signalling and nervous systems in animals"
}
